# Line endings.
#
# The repository had drifted: 134 text files were stored with LF and 8 with
# CRLF, so an ordinary edit to one of the CRLF files could rewrite every line of
# it depending on the editor and on whether the author had core.autocrlf set.
# That turns a two-line change into a thousand-line diff and makes `git blame`
# useless for the file.
#
# `text=auto` puts the decision in the repository rather than in each machine's
# git config: everything git recognises as text is stored with LF, and Windows
# checkouts still get CRLF in the working tree via core.autocrlf.
* text=auto

# Files whose content must survive byte-for-byte.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.db   binary

# Shell scripts are run by tools that reject CR, whatever the platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
